IMPORT prelude

-- Payment and Settlement Systems (Finality and Netting) Act 2002 (Singapore) -- designation and revocation (ss 3, 4), holding out
-- (s 4A), Part 2 finality against the law of insolvency (ss 6, 7, 8(3), (4), 12), netting on insolvency (s 13), foreign insolvency
-- orders (s 14), the duties to inform and notify (ss 15A, 15B, 16), composition (s 17), protection from liability (s 17C),
-- approval of Rules (s 19A) and written directions (s 20A), with the Authority's own exemption (s 5(2)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition ("incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"), informal consolidation
-- (version in force from 9/3/2025), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/PSSFNA2002.txt. The latest amendment annotated is
-- [Act 5 of 2025 wef 09/03/2025] on s 19(2) and (2A). Section numbers follow the BODY of the deposit; the arrangement of sections
-- at the top of the deposit is out of step with it (its labels are shifted against the numbers).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0111 (subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl): tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. SCOPED to what a participant, operator, settlement institution or collateral holder of a designated system meets.
-- Not encoded: the definitions in s 2 beyond what the rules use, the Authority's order-making under s 5(1), the specific IRDA
-- provisions disapplied by ss 9 and 10, the treatment of the net sum under s 11, preservation of underlying rights (s 15), the
-- attribution rules in ss 17A and 17B, District Court jurisdiction (s 18), delegation (s 19), regulations (s 20), exemptions
-- (s 20B) and the deemed designation of the old MAS system (s 21). No regulations or Gazette orders were retrieved, so which
-- systems are designated and which offences are compoundable are unknown here.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Payment and Settlement Systems (Finality and Netting) Act 2002`

§§ `3 -- designation of a system`

-- s 3(1): the Authority "may, by order in the Gazette, designate a system" if satisfied that a disruption in its operations may
-- "(a) trigger, cause or transmit disruption to other participants; (b) trigger or cause systemic disruption to the financial
-- system of Singapore; or (c) affect public confidence in the payment systems of Singapore or in the financial system".
-- (2) the order must specify the operator and settlement institution and "has effect until the order is revoked".
GIVEN `disruption may spread to other participants` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disruption may cause systemic disruption` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disruption may affect public confidence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may designate the system` IF
        `disruption may spread to other participants`
    OR  `disruption may cause systemic disruption`
    OR  `disruption may affect public confidence`

§§ `4 -- revocation and the right to be heard`

-- s 4(1) grounds: (a)(i) ceased to operate; (ii) operator "knowingly furnished" false or misleading information; (iii) operator or
-- settlement institution being wound up; (iv) compromise or scheme with creditors; (v) receiver, judicial manager or equivalent
-- appointed; (b) no longer systemic; (c) public interest. (2) "the Authority must not revoke a designation without giving the
-- operator ... an opportunity to be heard"; (3) except on grounds (a)(iii), (iv) or (v). (4) revocation does not avoid any
-- transaction cleared or settled before it.
DECLARE `Revocation ground` IS ONE OF
    `the system ceased to operate`
    `the operator knowingly gave false information`
    `the operator or settlement institution is being wound up`
    `a compromise or scheme with creditors`
    `a receiver or judicial manager was appointed`
    `the system is no longer systemically important`
    `the public interest`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Revocation ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator must be heard before revocation` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the operator or settlement institution is being wound up` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a compromise or scheme with creditors` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a receiver or judicial manager was appointed` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4A -- holding out as operator or settlement institution`

-- s 4A(1): a person "must not hold out that the person is an operator or a settlement institution of a designated system, unless"
-- (a) it is the operator or settlement institution of a system and (b) the Authority has designated that system.
GIVEN `holds out as operator of a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is the operator of the system` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the system is designated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holding out is an offence` IF
    `holds out as operator of a designated system` AND (NOT (`is the operator of the system` AND `the system is designated`))

§§ `6, 7, 12 -- finality of transfers against the law of insolvency`

-- s 6(2): Part 2 "applies in relation to bankruptcy, judicial management and winding up proceedings only in respect of a
-- participant"; (3) it does not apply to such proceedings "in respect of any person who is not a participant".
-- s 7(1)-(2): where the Rules of a designated system provide that a transfer into or out of a participant's account, a netting
-- or settlement of a payment obligation, or a settlement of book-entry securities "is final and irrevocable", then "despite
-- anything to the contrary in any written law or rule of law" it "must not be reversed, repaid or set aside and no order is to be
-- made by any court for the rectification or stay" of it.
-- s 12: Part 2 "does not apply in relation to any transfer order given by a participant which is entered into a designated system
-- after the expiry of one business day after" (a) a bankruptcy, judicial management or winding up order, (b) a judicial
-- management resolution under IRDA s 94(11), or (c) a voluntary winding up resolution.
-- The day count is an INFERENCE: 0 = entered on the business day of the event (or before it), 1 = the next business day.
-- Entry on business day 2 or later is "after the expiry of one business day after" the event.
DECLARE `Insolvency event` IS ONE OF
    `no insolvency event`
    `a bankruptcy order`
    `a winding up order`
    `a judicial management order`
    `a judicial management resolution`
    `a voluntary winding up resolution`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN `Insolvency event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `there is an insolvency event` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `no insolvency event` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `designated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a participant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the event` IS AN `Insolvency event`,
      `business days from the event to entry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 2 protects the transfer order` IF
        `designated`
    AND (    (NOT `there is an insolvency event` `the event`)
         OR  (`a participant` AND `business days from the event to entry` AT MOST 1))

GIVEN `designated` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Rules make it final and irrevocable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a participant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the event` IS AN `Insolvency event`,
      `business days from the event to entry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the transfer may be reversed or set aside` IF
    NOT (    `the Rules make it final and irrevocable`
         AND `Part 2 protects the transfer order` `designated` `a participant` `the event` `business days from the event to entry`)

§§ `8(3), (4) -- proof and set-off wait for the default arrangements`

-- s 8(3): a debt arising out of a transfer order "which is the subject of action taken under default arrangements may not be
-- proved in a bankruptcy or winding up until the completion of the action"; (4) nor "taken into account for the purposes of any
-- set-off" until then.
GIVEN `subject to default action` IS A BOOLEAN, `the default action is complete` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the debt may now be proved or set off` IF
    (NOT `subject to default action`) OR `the default action is complete`

§§ `13 -- netting on bankruptcy or winding up`

-- s 13: "Despite any provision of the law of insolvency", if a court has made an order for bankruptcy or winding up of a
-- participant "or a resolution for the voluntary winding up" has been passed, (a) the operator "may effect the netting of all
-- obligations owed to or by the participant incurred up to and including one business day after" the order or resolution;
-- (b) netted obligations are disregarded in the proceedings; (c) the net obligation is payable to the participant for the
-- creditors or provable; (d) the netting and payments under it are "not voidable".
-- Judicial management is NOT listed in s 13, though it is in ss 12 and 16.
GIVEN `the event` IS AN `Insolvency event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event triggers section 13 netting` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `a bankruptcy order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a winding up order` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a voluntary winding up resolution` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the event` IS AN `Insolvency event`, `business days from the event to the obligation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator may net the obligation under section 13` IF
    `the event triggers section 13 netting` `the event` AND `business days from the event to the obligation` AT MOST 1

§§ `14 -- foreign insolvency orders`

-- s 14: a court "is not to recognise or give effect to" a foreign insolvency order or the act of a foreign office holder "insofar
-- as the making of the order or doing of the act would be prohibited under this Act for a court in Singapore or a relevant office
-- holder".
GIVEN `it would be prohibited for a Singapore court or office holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Singapore court may give effect to the foreign order` IF
    NOT `it would be prohibited for a Singapore court or office holder`

§§ `15B, 16 and 5(2) -- duties to notify`

-- s 15B(1): a participant, operator, settlement institution or collateral holder of a designated system "must notify the Authority"
-- as soon as practicable if "(a) the person becomes, or is likely to become, insolvent or unable to meet the person's obligations"
-- (or a prescribed or directed event); (2) not if it "has already notified the Authority, under any other written law administered
-- by the Authority". (3) fine up to $200,000.
-- s 5(2): the Authority is exempt from s 15B (and 15A, 16, 19A, 20A) when it acts as a participant, operator, settlement institution
-- or collateral holder.
GIVEN `holds a role in a designated system` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is or is likely to become insolvent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `already notified under another MAS law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is the Authority itself` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must notify the Authority` IF
        `holds a role in a designated system`
    AND `is or is likely to become insolvent`
    AND (NOT `already notified under another MAS law`)
    AND (NOT `is the Authority itself`)

-- s 16(1): a participant "must notify the operator of a designated system as soon as practicable" after a bankruptcy, judicial
-- management or winding up order, a judicial management resolution under IRDA s 94(11), or a voluntary winding up resolution.
-- (2) fine up to $20,000. (3) no contravention if "(a) the participant took reasonable steps to comply" or "(b) the operator ... was
-- already aware of the relevant event".
GIVEN `the event` IS AN `Insolvency event`,
      `notified the operator` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `took reasonable steps to comply` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the operator was already aware` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to notify the operator is an offence` IF
        `there is an insolvency event` `the event`
    AND (NOT `notified the operator`)
    AND (NOT `took reasonable steps to comply`)
    AND (NOT `the operator was already aware`)

§§ `15A(5) -- the individual answerable for compliance`

-- s 15A(5): where a relevant person is guilty of an offence under (3) or (4), "any individual who is charged with the duty of
-- securing the relevant person's compliance ... and is in a position to discharge that duty, shall also be guilty".
GIVEN `the relevant person is guilty under 15A(3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `charged with securing compliance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in a position to discharge that duty` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the individual is also guilty under section 15A(5)` IF
        `the relevant person is guilty under 15A(3) or (4)`
    AND `charged with securing compliance`
    AND `in a position to discharge that duty`

§§ `19A -- Rules need the Authority's written approval`

-- s 19A(1): an operator, settlement institution or collateral holder "must, before implementing or amending any Rules of the
-- designated system, obtain the written approval of the Authority". (5) fine up to $200,000 and $20,000 a day continuing.
-- (6) Rules implemented "before 6 June 2018" are "deemed ... to be implemented with the written approval of the Authority".
GIVEN `implements or amends Rules` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `has written approval` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `implemented before 6 June 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `implementing the Rules is an offence` IF
        `implements or amends Rules`
    AND (NOT `has written approval`)
    AND (NOT `implemented before 6 June 2018`)

§§ `17C -- protection from liability`

-- s 17C(1): "No liability shall be incurred by a relevant person for anything done ... or omitted to be done with reasonable care
-- and in good faith" under the Act or the Rules. (2) "relevant person": an operator, settlement institution or collateral holder, or
-- an officer or employee of one. Participants are not in the list.
GIVEN `is an operator, settlement institution or collateral holder, or its officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `acted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `protected from liability` IF
        `is an operator, settlement institution or collateral holder, or its officer or employee`
    AND `acted with reasonable care`
    AND `acted in good faith`

§§ `4A(2), 15A, 15B(3), 16(2), 19A(5), 20A(6), 17 -- penalties and composition`

-- s 4A(2): $100,000 or 2 years or both; further $10,000 a day continuing after conviction.
-- s 15A(3): failing without reasonable excuse to comply with an information notice -- $150,000; further $15,000 a day.
-- s 15A(4): knowingly or recklessly false or misleading information -- $150,000.
-- s 15A(5): the individual answerable -- (a) wilfully, $125,000 or 12 months or both; (b) otherwise, $125,000.
-- s 15A(6): failing to take reasonable care over accuracy -- $15,000.
-- s 15B(3): $200,000.  s 16(2): $20,000.  s 19A(5): $200,000; further $20,000 a day.  s 20A(6): $150,000; further $15,000 a day.
-- s 17(1): the Authority may compound an offence "prescribed as a compoundable offence" by collecting "a sum of money not exceeding
-- half of the amount of the maximum fine prescribed for that offence". Which offences are prescribed was not retrieved. Whether the
-- daily further fine counts toward "the maximum fine" is not said; this encoding halves the base fine only (an INFERENCE).
-- `the maximum total fine` adds the daily fine for each day of continuation after conviction (a modelling choice: the Act states
-- the two as separate maxima).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `holding out as operator`
    `failing to comply with an information notice`
    `giving false information knowingly or recklessly`
    `individual answerable, wilfully`
    `individual answerable, not wilfully`
    `giving inaccurate information carelessly`
    `failing to notify the Authority`
    `failing to notify the operator`
    `implementing Rules without approval`
    `failing to comply with a written direction`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `holding out as operator` THEN 100000
    WHEN `failing to comply with an information notice` THEN 150000
    WHEN `giving false information knowingly or recklessly` THEN 150000
    WHEN `individual answerable, wilfully` THEN 125000
    WHEN `individual answerable, not wilfully` THEN 125000
    WHEN `giving inaccurate information carelessly` THEN 15000
    WHEN `failing to notify the Authority` THEN 200000
    WHEN `failing to notify the operator` THEN 20000
    WHEN `implementing Rules without approval` THEN 200000
    WHEN `failing to comply with a written direction` THEN 150000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further fine per day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `holding out as operator` THEN 10000
    WHEN `failing to comply with an information notice` THEN 15000
    WHEN `implementing Rules without approval` THEN 20000
    WHEN `failing to comply with a written direction` THEN 15000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `holding out as operator` THEN 24
    WHEN `individual answerable, wilfully` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum total fine` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` PLUS `the further fine per day` `the offence` TIMES `days continued after conviction`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most the Authority may collect to compound` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` DIVIDED BY 2
